#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:1
msgid "UCM Contributing Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:3
msgid ""
"Thank you for your interest in contributing to the UCM project! Our "
"community is open to all, and we welcome various contributions—your "
"efforts help the project grow and benefit more users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:4
msgid "🧩 Ways to Contribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:5
msgid ""
"You can contribute in the following ways, and we value each type of "
"participation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:6
msgid ""
"**🐛 Report issues or bugs**   Report any issues or unexpected behavior "
"you encounter. Your feedback helps us improve stability and performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:8
msgid ""
"**⚙️ Add support for new hardware or components**   Extend UCM to new "
"devices or platforms by proposing requirements or submitting "
"implementations. All ideas and contributions are welcome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:10
msgid ""
"**✨ Suggest or implement new features**   Share feature ideas or "
"contribute code to help UCM better meet user needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:12
msgid ""
"**📚 Improve documentation and guides**   Enhance existing documentation "
"or create new guides to help others get started quickly and effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:15
msgid "Every contribution matters—thank you for being part of the UCM community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:18
msgid "📄 License"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:20
msgid ""
"License information is available in the [LICENSE](https://github.com"
"/ModelEngine-Group/unified-cache-management/blob/develop/LICENSE) file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:23
msgid "🐞 How to Submit an Issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:25
msgid ""
"If you find a bug or want to suggest a new feature, please first check "
"[existing issues](https://github.com/ModelEngine-Group/unified-cache-"
"management/issues). If it’s a new issue, please [open a new "
"issue](https://github.com/ModelEngine-Group/unified-cache-"
"management/issues/new/choose   ) and include the following information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:27
msgid "**Title**: A clear and concise summary of the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:28
msgid ""
"**Environment**: Device, inference framework version, package version, "
"OS, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:29
msgid ""
"**Steps to Reproduce**: Clear, numbered steps to reliably trigger the "
"issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:30
msgid ""
"**Expected vs. Actual Behavior**: What should happen versus what actually"
" happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:31
msgid "**Error Messages / Logs**: Relevant console output or log snippets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:32
msgid "**Visual Evidence** (if helpful): Screenshots or short screen recordings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:33
msgid "**Severity**: Indicate impact level (*Critical*, *High*, *Medium*, *Low*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:35
msgid ""
"Keep your report clear, factual, and concise—this helps us address your "
"issue faster!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:38
msgid "💻 Submitting Code Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:39
msgid ""
"**To submit your code changes, please follow the workflow outlined "
"below.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:40
msgid "Step 1: Fork the Repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:42
msgid ""
"Fork the [UCM repository](https://github.com/ModelEngine-Group/unified-"
"cache-management) to your GitHub account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:44
msgid "Step 2: Create a Branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:46
msgid "Create a new branch with a clear and descriptive name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:48
msgid "Step 3: Implement Your Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:50
msgid ""
"Make your code or documentation changes in the branch, keeping them "
"focused and consistent with the project’s style and conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:52
msgid "Step 4: Run Lint Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:54
msgid "**UCM adheres to standard style conventions:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:56
msgid "Python code: [PEP 8](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:57
msgid ""
"C++ code: [Google C++ Style "
"Guide](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:59
msgid ""
"**The following tools help keep the codebase clean and consistently "
"formatted:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:61
msgid ""
"Python linting and formatting: "
"[black](https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/the_black_code_style) and "
"[isort](https://pycqa.github.io/isort/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:62
msgid ""
"Spell checking: [codespell](https://github.com/codespell-"
"project/codespell)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:63
msgid ""
"C++ formatting: [clang-"
"format](https://clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangFormat.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:65
msgid ""
"It’s recommended to set up a local development environment and run the "
"linter before submitting a PR to help ensure consistent code style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:67
msgid "**Run lint locally:** run code style checks and fix any issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:89
msgid "Step 5: Open a Pull Request (PR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:91
msgid ""
"Push your changes to your fork and open a PR in the main repository. "
"Include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:93
msgid "A **clear title** and **description** of your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:94
msgid "A reference to the related issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:95
msgid "Any additional context or screenshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:97
msgid ""
"The PR title is prefixed appropriately to indicate the type of change, "
"according to the following categories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:99
msgid ""
"💡 **Reminder:** If your PR spans multiple categories, include all "
"relevant prefixes (e.g., `[Feat][Test]`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:101
msgid "[Feat] for new features or enhancements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:102
msgid "[Bugfix] for bug fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:103
msgid ""
"[Opt] for code optimizations that improve performance, efficiency, or "
"resource usage without changing functionality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:104
msgid ""
"[Build] for build system changes, dependency updates, or tooling "
"improvements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:105
msgid "[CI] for continuous integration configuration and workflow updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:106
msgid "[Doc] for documentation improvements or corrections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:107
msgid "[Test] for adding, updating, or refactoring tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:108
msgid "[Misc] for PRs that do not fit other categories — please use sparingly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:110
msgid "Step 6: Code Review Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:112
msgid ""
"All pull requests targeting protected branches (e.g., `develop;release`) "
"must adhere to the following review policy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:114
msgid ""
"**Code Owner Approval Required**: Pull requests automatically request "
"reviews from relevant code owners based on the files changed. You cannot "
"approve your own pull request, and approval from at least one designated "
"code owner is mandatory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:115
msgid ""
"**Additional Approvals**: The pull request must receive sufficient peer "
"review beyond the author, including validation from maintainers or "
"experienced contributors familiar with the affected code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:116
msgid ""
"**Passing CI Checks**: All continuous integration checks—including "
"linting, unit tests, and builds—must pass before merging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:117
msgid ""
"**No Bypassing**: Direct pushes to protected branches are disabled, and "
"force merges or self-approvals are not permitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:119
msgid ""
"Once all requirements are satisfied, the “Squash and merge” button will "
"become available. Please ensure your changes are well-documented, tested,"
" and aligned with the project’s coding standards before requesting "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:121
msgid "📚 Improving Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:123
msgid "**Great docs grow stronger together. You can help by:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:125
msgid "Fixing typos or clarifying unclear text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:126
msgid "Documenting missing features or setup steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:127
msgid "Improving examples or adding practical use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:129
msgid "Building the docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:143
msgid "Review the documentation in your browser before submitting a pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contribute.md:145
msgid "English version: [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000/)"
msgstr ""

